{Presiding: Committee Chair; Member for Holhudhoo constituency Abdul Sattar Mohamed}

Statement by the Chair:

In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Assalaamu alaikum. I welcome all the honourable members to the 11th meeting of the Judiciary Committee of the People's Majlis. As you will know, according to today's agenda, this meeting follows an earlier decision of the committee to summon members of the Bar Council, in connection with members' concerns and with letters sent by some students regarding the amendment the Bar Council has proposed to the criteria for students currently studying law; regarding such concerns, the committee decided to summon members of the Council to clarify further information after obtaining information from the Bar Council. So this is a meeting held for that purpose. The members of the Bar Council will now be present. If the honourable members do not object, to save time, I intend to give the Bar Council members an opportunity to speak and then open the floor to members. That way you will also get more information, it will save time and it will be easier. For the information of all honourable members, the Secretariat has informed that the Bar Council's letter and the letters sent by students have been shared. So I request that the Bar Council members be brought in. Yes! Thank you. (After a short pause) In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Assalaamu alaikum. A very warm welcome to all the members of the Bar Council. Thank you for attending in response to our request, following a decision of the Judiciary Committee, that you appear here. According to today's agenda of our committee, the discussion today will be only on the matter on the agenda. Our time is one and a half hours unless the committee decides otherwise. To save time, I will announce, for the information of all honourable members and for the record, everyone who is present. I am doing it this way because I think it will be quicker. We will proceed with this meeting by first giving you, the Bar Council members, the opportunity, and after your remarks I will open the floor to members. According to the agenda,
